> the culture \" to adequately <ei18 service> high-net-worth individuals , he <ei19 adds> . U.S. Trust recently <ei21 introduced> certain mutual-fund products , which allow it to <ei22 serve> customers with minimum deposits of $ 250,000 . Previously , the company <ei23 advertised> at the $ 2 million level . \" We have always <ei24 taken> smaller accounts , but now we are <ei26 looking> for smaller accounts that will grow , \" Mr. Schwarz <ei27 says> . \" Our bread and butter is still the $ 2 million to $ 20 million account , \" he <ei28 says> . The new services <ei29 allow> U.S. Trust to <ei30 cater> to the \" new wealth , \" Mr. Schwarz <ei31 says> . Quarterly net income this year has <ei34 risen> just over comparable periods in 1988 , when year-end net was <ei36 below> the 1987 level . In this year 's third quarter , for example , net was $ 10.5 million , or $ 1.05 a share , compared with $ 10.3 million , or $ 1.02 a share , a year earlier . Assets as of Sept . 30 <ei41 fell> to $ 2.46 billion from about $ 2.77 billion . \" We will <ei42 have> a reasonably flat year this year , \" Mr. Schwarz <ei44 says> . Mr. Schwarz also <ei45 said> costs associated with U.S. Trust 's planned move to midtown Manhattan from Wall Street will <ei46 continue> to be a <ei47 drag> on earnings through 1990 . Mr. Schwarz 's great-grandfather <ei49 founded> the New York toy store F.A.O. Schwarz , but his family no longer <ei50 has> ties to the company . Mr. Schwarz 's father was a U.S. Trust <ei51 trustee> until 1974 . U.S. Trust also <ei53 created> a four-member office of the chairman , effective Feb . 1 . It will include Messrs . Schwarz and Maurer . Donald M. Roberts , 54 , treasurer , and Frederick S. Wonham , 58 , who takes responsibility for the funds-service group , were <ei55 named> vice chairmen and will <ei56 serve> in the office of the chairman . Mr. Roberts <ei57 continues> as <ei58 treasurer> , and Mr. Wonham <ei59 remains> <ei60 responsible> for the offices of comptroller , planning , marketing and general services . Frederick B. Taylor , 48 , also was <ei61 named> a vice chairman and chief investment <ei62 officer> , a new post . He previously <ei63 held> similar responsibilities . Mr. Taylor also was <ei64 named> a <ei65 director> , <ei66 increasing> the board to 22 , but is not part of the new office of the chairman . James E. Bacon , 58 , executive vice president , who has <ei67 directed> the funds-service group , will <ei68 retire> .", "gold": [["ei21", "causes", "ei22"], ["ei22", "causedby", "ei21"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei4", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei21", "ei22", "ei23", "ei24", "ei26", "ei27", "ei28", "ei29", "ei30", "ei31", "ei34", "ei36", "ei41", "ei42", "ei44", "ei45", "ei46", "ei47", "ei49", "ei50", "ei51", "ei53", "ei55", "ei56", "ei57", "ei58", "ei59", "ei60", "ei61", "ei62", "ei63", "ei64", "ei65", "ei66", "ei67", "ei68"], "surfaces": {"ei1": "named", "ei2": "succeed", "ei4": "reaches", "ei5": "succeeded", "ei6": "faced", "ei7": "established", "ei8": "promoted", "ei10": "hurt", "ei11": "welcomes", "ei12": "calling", "ei13": "says", "ei14": "broadens", "ei15": "dealing", "ei16": "believe", "ei17": "have", "ei18": "service", "ei19": "adds", "ei21": "introduced", "ei22": "serve", "ei23": "advertised", "ei24": "taken", "ei26": "looking", "ei27": "says", "ei28": "says", "ei29": "allow", "ei30": "cater", "ei31": "says", "ei34": "risen", "ei36": "below", "ei41": "fell", "ei42": "have", "ei44": "says", "ei45": "said", "ei46": "continue", "ei47": "drag", "ei49": "founded", "ei50": "has", "ei51": "trustee", "ei53": "created", "ei55": "named", "ei56": "serve", "ei57": "continues", "ei58": "treasurer", "ei59": "remains", "ei60": "responsible", "ei61": "named", "ei62": "officer", "ei63": "held", "ei64": "named", "ei65": "director", "ei66": "increasing", "ei67": "directed", "ei68": "retire"}, "sentence_of": {"ei1": 0, "ei2": 1